%U A174319 211059485310,861083848998,3516072837894,14334995983614,58485689950254,238306751550942,971603790333342,3956948440885134,16123562844550038
%N A174319 Number of n-step self-avoiding walks on the simple cubic lattice having no pair of nonconsecutive vertices that are adjacent in the lattice.
%C A174319 Fisher and Hiley give 2674926 as their last term instead of 2675022 (see A002934). Douglas McNeil confirms the correction on the seqfan list.
%C A174319 In the notation of Nemirovsky et al. (1992), a(n), the n-th term of the current sequence is C_{n,m} with m=0 (and d=3). Here, for a d-dimensional hypercubic lattice, C_{n,m} is "the number of configurations of an n-bond self-avoiding chain with m neighbor contacts." (Let n >= 1. For d=2, we have C(n,0) = A173380(n); for d=4, we have C(n,0) = A034006(n); and for d=5, we have C(n,0) = A038726(n).) - _Petros Hadjicostas_, Jan 03 2019
%C A174319 From _Carlo Corti_, Aug 20 2026: (Start)
%C A174319 Previous name was: Number of n-step walks on cubic lattice (no points repeated, no adjacent points unless consecutive in path).
%C A174319 The walks are rooted at a fixed lattice vertex; rotations, reflections, and reversal are counted as distinct. (End)
%D A174319 N. J. A. Sloane, A Handbook of Integer Sequences, Academic Press, 1973 (includes this sequence).
%D A174319 N. J. A. Sloane and Simon Plouffe, The Encyclopedia of Integer Sequences, Academic Press, 1995 (includes this sequence).
%H A174319 Carlo Corti, <a href="/A174319/b174319.txt">Table of n, a(n) for n = 0..27</a>
%H A174319 M. E. Fisher and B. J. Hiley, <a href="https://doi.org/10.1063/1.1731729">Configuration and free energy of a polymer molecule with solvent interaction</a>, J. Chem. Phys., 34 (1961), 1253-1267.
%H A174319 Y.-H. Hsieh, C.-N. Chen, and C.-K. Hu, <a href="https://doi.org/10.1051/epjconf/201610801005">Exact Partition Functions of Interacting Self-Avoiding Walks on Lattices</a>, EPJ Web Conf. 108 (2016), 01005.
%H A174319 Y.-H. Hsieh, C.-N. Chen, and C.-K. Hu, <a href="https://doi.org/10.1016/j.cpc.2016.08.006">Efficient algorithm for computing exact partition functions of lattice polymer models</a>, Comput. Phys. Commun. 209 (2016), 27-33.
%H A174319 A. M. Nemirovsky, K. F. Freed, T. Ishinabe, and J. F. Douglas, <a href="https://doi.org/10.1007/BF01049010">Marriage of exact enumeration and 1/d expansion methods: lattice model of dilute polymers</a>, J. Statist. Phys., 67 (1992), 1083-1108.
%F A174319 a(n) = 6 + 24*A038746(n) + 48*A038748(n) for n >= 1. (It follows from Eq. (5), p. 1090, in Nemirovsky et al. (1992).) - _Petros Hadjicostas_, Jan 01 2019
%F A174319 a(n) = 2 * A118339(n+1) for n>=1. - _Andrei Zabolotskii_, Apr 08 2026
%F A174319 a(n) = 6*Z_{n+1}(0) for n >= 1, where Z_N(x) is defined in Eq. (3) of the Hsieh, Chen, and Hu EPJ Web Conf. paper and in Eq. (2) of their Comput. Phys. Commun. paper; the factor 6 restores the six possible first-step directions suppressed by the fixed-direction convention used in both papers. - _Carlo Corti_, Aug 20 2026
%Y A174319 Cf. A038746, A038748, A118339.
